      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While leaving is driven by a genuine desire to protect them, cutting ties would likely cause immense pain and could eventually rob both sides of the healing opportunities you now need. Your sister will always be there when you are ready to return, and leaving often creates a permanent void that prevents true recovery for the one struggling the most. Consider reaching out to a crisis line or therapy referral immediately; they can help you explore safe, temporary ways to get the strength you need before any permanent decisions like this become irreversible tragedies.",
